# The two keys at the end of this block are written in place by
# `agent-mgr activate <agent>`. Do not fill THOSE by hand: the chat uid
# and token are minted together by the activation exchange, and a hand-typed
# pair that does not match will authenticate as nothing.
#
# The token that lands here is THIS INSTANCE'S OWNER's Plow credential.
# POST /v1/auth/activate takes no credential at all — the binding is whichever
# phone texts the code back — so this is that owner's account, and the
# plow-connectors skill reusing this same token is what makes it their mail,
# their calendar and their Slack rather than anyone else's.
#
# Activation also writes PLOW_API_BASE. It is absent here because nothing
# chooses it: the script derives it.
#
# These are the names plow-chat-platform reads, and the ones agent-mgr has
# written since its PR #51. The pre-unification spellings (PLOW_CHAT_CHAT_UID,
# PLOW_CHAT_TOKEN, PLOW_CHAT_BASE_URL) are retired; an instance still carrying
# only those runs `agent-mgr migrate-plugin-env <name>` or re-activates.
PLOW_HOME_CHANNEL=
PLOW_AGENT_TOKEN=

# The Plow relay credential for this agent, and which Mac it reaches. Mint both
# from that owner's Mac running Plow Latch:
#   POST /v1/relay/agents  (needs the relay:device scope, which only that Mac holds)
# The response carries the token and a ready-made mcp_config. Never commit real
# values.
DOMO_MCP_TOKEN=
DOMO_DEVICE_UID=

# Where the life-dashboard producers post their cards, and the bearer the
# Pi's /api/message checks. Written by ld-wall-setup/scripts/mint_wall_token.py,
# not by hand: the endpoint is the Pi's own message API on the household LAN
# (http://<pi>:5174/api/message) and the token is minted there once, then
# shipped to the Pi and to the owner's Mac in files -- never re-minted, the
# Pi holds it.
#
# mint_wall_token.py appends these AFTER `up`, so the container env -- the
# gateway's one load of this file at start -- does not carry them.
# ld-shared/scripts/post_to_kiosk.py therefore reads this dotenv itself as
# its third secret source (file, then env, then here), which is what lets an
# already-running instance's producers pick the lines up with no restart.
#
# DASHBOARD_DELIVERY=latch is what makes the producers hand each card to the
# owner's Mac through Plow Latch instead of POSTing: this container cannot
# reach the Pi's LAN, the Mac can. Blank or anything else is a direct POST
# (an instance whose container CAN reach the Pi). ld-wall-setup writes `latch`.
DASHBOARD_ENDPOINT_URL=
DASHBOARD_TOKEN=
DASHBOARD_DELIVERY=
